{"title":"Topicwise Test-2 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Network-2","fileName":"073_Topicwise Test-2 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Network-2.html","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electronics Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider inductive coils having number of turns <em>N</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>N</em><sub>2</sub> are magnetically coupled to each other. If the number of turns of second coil is changed to <em>N</em>′<sub>2</sub> such that the mutual inductance between the coupled coils become half, then the ratio of <img src=\"/media/a6aef12cb0a7e9a7f5ea6d52c58b5b180fe83fc9.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 4</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.5</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 2</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.25</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/82a360cae4e9795d77b24e1269c5a81b0650c497.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In the given circuit, if the inductor is initially relaxed, then the current in the circuit will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/94874ea19cd113d3217c6ca7f1c9d433758a3811.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Zero</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/7ed37d9dca2c9de3e682e4bfa3e494ab73e29243.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/4a808123f7be4d50fb1edcdb4a0097d883630725.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/dcdab8b385ae0459aa5d05f29483d9a35da8be0b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/b516266b7bf0fb670e01f8db8a071e3de65754a3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Match List-I (2-port parameter) with List-II (Equivalent) and select the correct answer using the code given below the lists:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d42e52983cd1e76e6820c7c6bbafcd8f15504e64.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> a</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> b</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> c</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> d</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/44dd6627942f770ac7d9b0708fc179471127f1ae.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A two port network is symmetrical if</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <em>AD</em> – <em>BC</em> = 1</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><em>A</em> = <em>D</em></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p><em>Y</em><sub>21</sub> = <em>Y</em><sub>12</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <em>h</em><sub>11</sub><em>h</em><sub>22</sub> – <em>h</em><sub>12</sub><em>h</em><sub>21</sub> = –1</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/7fa0f7b4204d87347b1bfc28d9fd89a91a5fea8b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For DC supply, a uncharged inductor, <img src=\"/media/39bd006d980afcf132dafba2c943ffdfd5acc472.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> will act as a</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/6e1e930b4324a4b8c028cc0de6dd4c0c69bf3f72.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/854f00426fcf20a701da3c3fab2b9ba00c23811d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> It depends on the circuit to circuit</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of the above</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nFor DC source,<br />\nAn uncharged inductor will act as open circuit element whereas, a fully charged inductor will act as short circuit.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below, if <img src=\"/media/6fc775760c070fcb0dc00ebbf0ed34344f4dde1b.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> cos 500t A in the network, the total energy stored in the network is _______ Joules.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/eaec6534d03610626fea6105cde23b4000ca5905.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"64","high":"64"},"solution":"<p>64 (64 - 64)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/bb64f1b8b9bcddd3ccc416c48508788d654fce73.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f1f0518dfa0392ce0c2e88ae2aceb8dfc25e84ac.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The forward current gain with the output short-circuited is _________. (rounded off to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-0.56","high":"-0.56"},"solution":"<p>-0.56 (-0.58 - -0.55)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/7fa2ef9b86f1f4cb033ab7655dea82e8db6a09f0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A series R-L circuit has R = 10 Ω and <em>L</em> = 10 Henry. Assume the inductor to be initially uncharged. A d.c. voltage of 50 V is applied at <em>t</em> = 0. The voltage across inductor (L) at t = 2 sec is ________ V. (rounded off to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6.77","high":"6.77"},"solution":"<p>6.77 (6.75 - 6.78)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/3bbcf4088d4c32411ab2d7b3389c4a9206870512.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/42e67b89fb70a161bbe9e3c30f585d3461c6a871.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In the network shown below, the switch is moved from position 1 to 2 at <em>t</em> = 0</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f3cdc1dabe85ba3324f4a19df859bb4be3cbdb6b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Then, which of the following option(s) is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>The time constant of the circuit is <img src=\"/media/b16a45d7731ecac5e4f60a55ba2322bbc7ea8a3b.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> sec.</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>At <em>t</em> = 0<sup>+</sup>; the current across inductor is 2.67 A.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>The current equation for <img src=\"/media/8ff40b1939edc1bf0fddb1ac1379310d9a8fec35.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is (2.5 + 0.17e<sup>–8t</sup>)A</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>The current equation for <img src=\"/media/e6bd32bc69d3da9d73ab3b364425f08eeb29d436.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is (2.5 – 0.17e<sup>–8t</sup>) A</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/665461afbabba9923df6a1cd71ee3ab5cac90fc6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/bc4714de9f94beee35835b67885757323fdb4210.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>In the network shown in figure below, at <em>t</em> = 0, the switch is opened.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/25a9043a892b48241dde32461ab4269296e2edd1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"/media/192c6fd86ff47c0d88fb2075be1e69127b8557e8.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 101 MV</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 10 kV</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1 MV</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> –1 MV</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4c3d78621a9cf562d214e8669fc1da86fa028206.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/495e86ac5cb90058fe0fac8061a21c1b8f68991e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For the two port network <em>N</em> shown below in figure, Z parameter matrix is <img src=\"/media/d21225ea5157337491d1085d0e99c5c6803cbe38.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The value of <img src=\"/media/b3dbda072ae8e76e85de7a3bc3564f726ce155e1.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> in Amperes is approximately</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/487beb77aaa5ddd7d242f1e648deb6fd8c9cbe98.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1 A</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 6 A</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 4 A</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 5 A</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a0fcb1db48273106424eba919c5dbeb729efb073.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Two networks are connected in cascade as shown in figure. Transmission matrix for network <em>N</em><sub>1 </sub>is <img src=\"/media/99e7ef8d5b51ca972cf5973ad928d3b300fdecbd.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and the overall transmission matrix is <img src=\"/media/b4758d57767ccbd92373b3354163ad425acb7111.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/56c8558f035919811a1dcfae7bb06ebc7ced7c5b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The value of transmission parameter <em>C</em> for the network <em>N</em><sub>2</sub> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 4</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 5</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 8</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 3</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/53726cae7bb8069f27e738c24fc4a4c7f8296afe.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For the below given network,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f26992478f0d7a376b679a478215495b30e5cec8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The z-parameter Z<sub>12</sub> is given by</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <em>s</em></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 2<em>s</em></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.2<em>s</em></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/30773a1e4d59ab1bdb28416b83f91d1ed2dd50b8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d714f4e0d7a6450e550ccc44070374b6a863854d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In the network given below, the switch is initially at position 1. The steady state at position 1 is reached and the switch is changed to position 2 at <em>t</em> = 0.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/77ace17aed0c3e41641577d51979e18401fa573f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Then, the current across 5 H inductor at <em>t</em> = 5 sec is _________ μA. (correct to one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.6","high":"1.6"},"solution":"<p>1.60 (1.59 - 1.61)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c4bd0f8a4e40844570a70348688996bf1aebf4a8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/440ee27fa97dc05e59a639e24ff915504f1b0d2f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the network shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e17d0a54045a04103973725af089fe3c39397184.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The equivalent resistance across <em>A</em>-<em>B</em> is _________ Ω. (correct to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3.45","high":"3.45"},"solution":"<p>3.45 (3.40 - 3.50)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d998b56209611b15e5223d022a6de7085d539097.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/cb3b89a5b8567d006dcaf4ebc62583950242e531.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the given Star-Delta pair shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/279fd3f9e252ca4c2c7d869a732da18b37a5e71b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"/media/963405bae1cbe4c3f8d8e2d22035207affb93301.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is ________ μF. (correct to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"17.08","high":"17.08"},"solution":"<p>17.08 (17.04 - 17.14)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e2f7ad145e51fb0fa3acca72845ea4ad660b9b45.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A 10 μF capacitor and 5 kΩ resistor are connected in series across a 50 V battery at <em>t</em> = 0. Then, which of the following options is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> the instantaneous voltage across capacitor is <em>V<sub>c</sub></em>(<em>t</em>) = 50<em>e<sup>–20t</sup></em> V.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> at <em>t</em> = 1 sec; the voltage across capacitor is approximately 50 V.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> at <em>t</em> = 0.2 sec; the voltage across capacitor is approximately 6.77 V.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> the instantaneous voltage across capacitor is <em>V<sub>c</sub></em>(<em>t</em>) = 50(1 – <em>e<sup>–20t</sup></em>) V.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, d)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d3c803282401d451cf85903c9ea33986735b8ef2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:15.950Z"}